WEBVTT

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.530
"Sky" "Cloud"

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.530
"Trees"

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.010
Here goes.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.580
Bring it.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.570
--Aquarion!
--Aquarion!

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.930
Deava!

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.760
Logos!

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:10.500
<i>The world is engulfed by an unvoiced scream</i>

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:16.440
<i>and I wait for it to reach and stir</i> <i>a certain someone's heart</i>

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:22.240
<i>With strength flowing to the edges of our souls</i>

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:28.520
<i>we set out into the white</i> <i>morning haze, without hesitation</i>

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.450
<i>I want to know everything about you</i>

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:41.450
<i>But just when I thought</i>
<i>I had you, you were gone</i>

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.540
<i>It's love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:57.150
<i>These tightly-sealed, silent lips</i>

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.520
<i>gently reply back in kind</i>

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.790
<i>And with love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:12.290
<i>Now, from the last of the words I couldn't find,</i>

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:21.000
<i>the music begins</i>

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:35.880
"It Will Not End! Aquarion Logos"

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:45.390
"Traffic Light"

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.250
A-Akira is fighting!

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:45.390
"Tree"

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.560
Our voices. We need to send our voices to him once more!

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.390
Yeah, if we call out to him again, he'll win easily!

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.030
A-Akira, do your best!

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.400
Akira, don't you lose!

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.600
Mr. Savior!

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.900
You go show him...

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.400
...what Deava can do!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.240
I have no clue what's happening, but good luck!

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.510
We're cheering for you!

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.510
Go get him!

00:02:58.510 --> 00:02:59.770
You can do it!

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.410
Akira, fight hard!

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.780
Akira, it's time for you to save the world!

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:04.710
Let this reach you!

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.580
The voice of our souls--

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.850
No thanks.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:09.620
"Cutting External Audio"

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.130
"External Audio Cut"

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.800
Our voices aren't reaching him? Why?

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.710
They aren't listening to anyone.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.110
M-Maia.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.210
You had us worried!

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.380
You're okay?

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.880
Yeah.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.380
Thank goodness...

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:44.220
Oh, uh... Does that mean Akira's the only one piloting that Deava?

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.490
Then, the one piloting the other Aquarion must be...

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.330
Subete is piloting the Logos.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.160
The M.J.B.K. should have been defeated.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.100
Why are the two of them fighting?

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.270
No clue. They left me behind.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.070
What do you mean?

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:04.470
It's not for the world.
And it's not over someone like me.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:07.080
But those two will still fight.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.570
Wh-Why?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.510
Who knows? Because they're idiots, I guess.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:23.320
Sougon, Mao, are you watching?

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.990
Your son is becoming a man.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.370
Don't lose, Subete.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.110
Blow!

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:38.640
"Blow"

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:52.050
Burn!

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:51.720
"Fire"

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.050
Tear!

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.030
"Fire-blowing Slash"

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.690
Blade of Kagutsuchi!

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.140
It's lukewarm.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:11.970
It's a wonder that you managed to defeat the M.J.B.K. like that, Akira.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.540
If that's all, your chances of winning are zero!

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:15.870
"Zero"

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.380
"Absolute Zero"

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.540
Absolute zero!

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.870
This is awesome!

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.900
Hey, shouldn't we run away?

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.440
Where to?

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.000
Isn't this kind of awesome?

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.700
It's amazing! This is the real deal!

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:53.950
If it's a meaningless battle, shouldn't we stop them?

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.080
It does... have meaning.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.090
Hey, are you watching?

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.450
"Atsushi: Hey, are you watching?"

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.450
"Pon: I am!"

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:57.450
"Atsushi: Isn't it awesome?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:57.450
I wonder what they're doing."

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.220
I am!

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.120
"Atsushi: Isn't it awesome?

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.120
I wonder what they're doing."

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.120
"Chiroro: What are you talking about?

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.120
*munch* *munch*"

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.050
"Chiroro: What are you talking about?

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.050
*munch* *munch*"

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.050
"Pon: They're fighting

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.050
in the sky or something!!"

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.950
Isn't it awesome?
I wonder what they're doing.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.090
"Pon: They're fighting

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.090
in the sky or something!!"

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.090
"Chiroro: I just looked outside.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.090
Are they shooting a movie?"

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:00.960
I just looked outside.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.720
--Hey! There's something super cool up in the sky!
--Are they shooting for a movie?

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:21.310
All the people of the world are watching over their battle now.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.310
You could say everyone's attention is being seized by this battle.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:30.270
To the point that they don't have time to direct hostility at other people.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:35.320
I see. For as long as everyone's attention is on the battle,

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.730
their feelings won't drive the written words to run amok.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:42.800
Th-Their fight is saving the world?

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:48.830
And with a stirring event like this, people want to tell someone about it.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:51.770
"yuka: Huh? What is it?"

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.770
"Rina: I'm watching right now! It's awesome."

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:10.860
"Buildings"

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:06.850
That strong wish to communicate will create a history we hand down

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.120
and someday form a legend.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:14.800
Yes, this is a legend unfolding before our very eyes!

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.830
President Kenzaki,
I've found my answer at last.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.270
I will continue to protect writing from here on.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:25.000
To record the way they lived in writing...

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.880
...and to tell it in my voice.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.180
Subete!

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.680
Akira!

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:59.970
That moonlit night, our fates parted ways, with Maia as an axis.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:04.080
Had our positions been reversed, would anything have changed?

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.750
Don't care.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:09.550
You're so boring. I can't stand you.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.710
And that's why you're there, isn't it?

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.050
You do get it!

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.160
Look at the moon!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.690
I will now put my everything on the line...

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.170
...and I will strike you down!

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:32.860
Reach him.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:37.210
This is my fist.

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:39.580
Let's settle this, Subete.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.110
Swallow everything!

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.110
"Moon Sword Multiverse"

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.120
Moon Sword Multiverse!

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:51.120
"Moon Sword Multiverse"

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.190
Burn to ashes!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.130
"Sun God Nova"

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:58.690
Sun God Nova!

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:58.630
"Sun God Nova"

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.890
Just... a little more...

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.770
Akira... I will defeat you!

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.740
Make way!

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:40.140
If you stand between me and the world,
I will overcome everything to get there!

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.960
It's so bright!

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.450
What happened?

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.290
M-Maia?

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.950
Subete!

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.440
Akira!

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.130
I've been meaning to say,
I bet you have no friends!

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:36.000
Like you can talk! Don't put me in the same boat as you!

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.670
I didn't need anyone! Or anything!

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:44.800
Being a savior was my sole reason to live!

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:48.680
What a boring life!

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:53.050
Are you going to live your whole life cursed by the word "savior"?

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.320
Cursed?!

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:59.150
Yeah, a curse. It limits your life choices.

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:00.820
Is that not a curse?!

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.830
You're annoying! Shut up!

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.420
No, you!

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.590
Tornado Strike!

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:16.770
Don't lose! You can do better than this, Vector-0!

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.500
Pierce through! Vector-Ga!

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:38.730
"Ground"

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:44.360
"Sky"

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:44.360
"Ground"

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.030
You...!

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:08.990
"Tree"

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:08.990
"Grass"

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:09.820
"Ground"

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.090
Gather!

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.480
Wait, Akira!

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:03.540
I won't wait!

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:09.550
You're my savior, aren't you?
Then protect me forever!

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.520
You're not supposed to up and vanish on me!

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.280
I'm sorry.

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.660
Tsukigane...

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.150
Akira...

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.390
"Sky"

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.390
"Trees"

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.640
He will take hold of love, dreams, and everything else.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:30.810
So, I named him "everything."

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:34.210
For you are the chosen one.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.040
Protect the one you love.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.310
Strike down your fated enemy.

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.520
Subete!

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:50.190
Verbalize!

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:51.930
Wait, Subete!

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:55.500
Sousei Gattai! Draw!

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.020
Aquarion Logos!

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.770
"Sky"

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.770
"Clouds"

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.930
"Leaf" "Tree" "Bush"

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.930
"Rock" "Ground"

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:21.620
What's happening?

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:27.530
The unstable wandering words are heading to the world where they belong.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:15:00.120
Yes, to the Logos World you've created.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.830
How does it feel, Akira?

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:10.740
The one who saved this world and Maia was me.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:19.980
Yes, Subete, you are the savior.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:22.620
"Love"

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:23.740
Victory is mine. Take that.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.740
Subete...

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:52.880
"NESTA New President's

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:52.880
Inaugural Press Conference"

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:42.940
Does that mean Nesta will provide its services as before, President Soda?

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:45.270
Yes, that is our intent.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.680
While it was to protect the world from an invasion of writing,

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:52.880
more than a few people feel wary of
Deava after they lied to the public.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:55.650
Given you are the former commander of that organization,

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:58.380
are you really an appropriate choice for company president?

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:09.830
"NESTA New President's

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:09.830
Inaugural Press Conference"

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:05.130
There are things I must do precisely because I misled the public.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:09.830
Winning trust is another valuable form of communication.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.700
Pamyun... I'm exhausted...

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.640
There's no time to relax.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.540
You have three meetings scheduled for this afternoon.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:22.140
You turned into a bully the moment you became my secretary!

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:26.550
You must have known being president would be difficult. Why did you accept?

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:32.250
I thought I could only prove it if I were here.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:35.490
That writing is necessary?

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:39.090
That writing can bring people happiness, I think.

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.200
"Open for Business

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:43.200
Please, come in!"

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.160
Pamyun!

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:45.570
Kokone, you're leaving?

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.770
Shoko will be lonely!

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:51.670
You don't have to imitate the manager just because you're the acting manager.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:51.710
"Please refrain from taking

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:51.710
pictures of the staff."

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:54.840
I thought I should carry on her spirit, at least.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:59.550
Anyway, Kikogami, are you sure about studying abroad?

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:05.850
"Verbalism Club

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:05.850
Outdoor Stage Performance

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:05.850
Hanako and Princess Kaguya"

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:05.850
Yeah. I want to study singing and acting in a different environment.

00:17:05.850 --> 00:17:08.090
Still, this is way too sudden!

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:09.460
Yeah!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:11.590
With the Logos World stabilized,

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:14.360
we won't need to fight in Aquarion anymore,

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:18.470
but Shirobaco's reading theater and singing are still ongoing to rave reviews!

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:21.040
We'll have a hard time without you here!

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:23.200
Stop it, you two.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.310
You decided this after thinking it through, I'm sure.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.800
Yeah.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:37.380
I... I realized I've lived in a very small world up until now...

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:41.880
My dreams, aspirations, feelings, all of it...

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:45.890
It was only things within arm's reach.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:46.960
Kokone!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.500
I won't cry!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:53.970
But, seeing Akira and
Tsutomu fight, I thought

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:57.300
the world expands out to infinity!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:01.280
It's a waste to just stay sitting here in one place.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:07.450
So, I want to see a wider world.
In order to move towards my dreams.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.420
You're amazing, Kokone.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:12.250
Huh? I'm... not amazing at all.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:16.290
Now you've got me fired up, too!

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:20.990
I'm going to move forward one step at a time until I'm a famous voice actor!

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.260
I can't let you all beat me.

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:27.600
Hayato, you mentioned Senator
Kobayakawa has been inviting you.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:29.870
He asked if you wanted to work as his secretary.

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:33.270
Wow! The secretary to the future Prime Minister!

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:36.280
No, I haven't decided for sure that I'll accept yet.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.110
Hey, hey, Big Brother Hayato.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:42.120
Once you're the PM's secretary, pull some political strings for me,

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:45.520
so they'll cast Karan Uminagi as the lead voice in a major movie!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.520
Weren't you going to go step by step?

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.290
Hey, I've been wondering for a while now...

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:52.290
What is that?

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.890
Oh, this?

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:57.300
The Verbalism Club's activities will keep on going.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:02.540
With that in mind, there's someone we need to never forget.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.470
You mean...

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:07.510
It's inevitable that the memory of him will fade with time...

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:11.680
So, at the very least, I want to leave something physical.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.340
Can we put up a statue of him in the shop?

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:18.690
Yeah, no.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:21.190
Sorry, Big Brother, this is awful.

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:22.190
N-No!

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:23.360
Not happening.

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.330
Yeah, seriously, no way.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.200
I see. Not happening, huh?

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.670
Tsutomu...

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:42.180
"Tokyo Prison"

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:38.210
Hey, you, what is it you're always writing?

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:43.680
A memoir. Not my own, though.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:46.850
You're writing someone else's reflections, then?

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:49.180
It's not just a reflection.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:53.190
This is the tale of a father and son trapped by love

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:56.690
who seized the past and struggled to create the future...

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:58.790
You could call it their legend.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:03.360
I don't get it, but it sounds like you're writing something big and important.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.030
If you get it published, tell me the title.

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:08.530
I'll buy ten copies, Mr. Literary Genius.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.940
A title, huh?

00:20:12.070 --> 00:20:16.880
"The Legend of Subete

00:20:12.070 --> 00:20:16.880
Aquarion Logos"

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.880
<i>Aquarion Logos</i>. How does that sound?

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:22.880
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:38.270
<i>With the warmth of salvation,</i>
<i>I raise my hand into the sky</i>

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:43.000
<i>and everything in the world gains its true colors</i>

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.670
<i>(Focus) A sound that was once hidden</i>

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:48.780
<i>(on the goal) will connect us now</i>

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:51.280
<i>Try to understand that, okay?</i>

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:53.750
<i>So, are you ready?</i>

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:56.520
<i>(heart and soul) These silent teardrops</i>

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.120
<i>(narrow escape) that flow forth now</i>

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:02.620
<i>(enamored) are proof of that person's existence</i>

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:09.130
<i>You can't go inside your heart all alone</i>

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:11.700
<i>I will hesitate no more</i>

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:16.870
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:22.110
<i>A useful life, a sparkling utopia</i>

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:31.180
<i>When your heart and voice</i> <i>tremble together, you'll surpass all</i>

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:34.620
<i>So go for your heart</i>

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.970
Someone!

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:07.320
--Ow!
--P-Police!

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.590
Call the police, quick!

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:10.760
Thank you.

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:13.430
You're amazing. How did you do that?

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:18.500
If there are voices seeking salvation,
I will always be there to extend a hand.

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:19.990
For I am...

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:27.740
What was with that guy?

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:30.940
He seemed nice, but kind of a weirdo.

00:22:30.940 --> 00:22:34.440
Yeah, he might be a weirdo! A weirdo!

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.680
What are you doing?

00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:41.890
That moonlit night,

00:22:41.890 --> 00:22:45.530
I decided to become a savior for your sake.

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:50.020
Even after I forgot you, being a savior was all I had inside me.

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:53.370
But...

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:57.360
Ultimately, he was the one who saved you, and this world, and became the savior.

00:22:59.070 --> 00:23:01.410
Subete, huh?

00:23:01.410 --> 00:23:06.210
My reason to live... My curse...
He took it all away.

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:11.710
I'm empty now. I have nothing.

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:17.250
What should I live for from here on?

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:25.670
They called you a weirdo.
Did you notice that?

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:31.910
"Weirdo"

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:33.140
I told you, my feelings for you gave me a heart that made me human.

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:34.630
So...

00:23:37.610 --> 00:23:40.910
...this time, I will give you a heart.

00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:41.850
"Lover"

00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:06.100
The train bound for Takao will soon arrive on Platform 1.

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:10.840
"Aquarion Logos"
